; expr-env: the time-environment bindings that expr-control does not
; already pin — bpm, dur (bound only when the transport declares :dur),
; and cycle (the Pattern alias of bar). dur is in BEATS, so :dur 2bar at
; 120 bpm 4/4 gives dur = 8; bpm = 120; cycle counts bars continuously.
; Each track isolates one binding so the golden reads them apart, and a
; fourth combines all three to pin them under arithmetic.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4] :dur 2bar)

(track :target tempo  :expr bpm)
(track :target length :expr dur)
(track :target turn   :expr cycle)
(track :target mix    :expr (/ (* cycle bpm) dur))
